In this paper, we propose a Sequence Labeling based Question Answering (SLQA) method to mine NL-PL pairs in a PL-agnostic manner. In particular, we propose to apply the BIO tagging scheme instead of the conventional binary scheme to mine the code solutions which are often composed of multiple blocks of a post. Experiments on current single-PL single-block benchmarks and a manually-labeled cross-PL multi-block benchmark prove the effectiveness and transferability of SLQA. We further present a parallel NL-PL corpus named Lang2Code automatically mined with SLQA, which contains about 1.4M pairs on 6 PLs. Under statistical analysis and downstream evaluation, we demonstrate that Lang2Code is a large-scale high-quality data resource for further NL-PL research.

