The PHT was first introduced by Ghrist \cite{arxivID-0905.4887-11} and has since been used in a range of applications, including: protein structural analysis \cite{arxivID-2410.08203-12}, plant morphology \cite{arxivID-1110.1509-13}, and brain cancer prediction \cite{arxivID-2004.11128-14}. The PHT has also been used in the context of topological data analysis \cite{arxivID-2303.14040-15}, where it has been shown to be stable to perturbations of the shape \cite{arxivID-2303.14040-16}. The PHT has also been generalized to the Euler Characteristic Transform (ECT), which is a more general topological summary of a shape \cite{arxivID-2004.11128-17, arxivID-2212.01666-18, arxivID-1705.02045-19, arxivID-2310.07630-20, arxivID-2310.10395-21}

