The Definition Generation (DG) task has been widely studied in recent years. Most of the previous studies are based on encoder-decoder models \cite{arxivID-1406.1078-6}. The encoder-decoder model is a sequence-to-sequence model, which encodes the source sentence into a fixed-length vector and then decodes the vector to generate the target sentence. The encoder-decoder model has achieved great success in the DG task \cite{arxivID-2205.04602-7, arxivID-2010.03124-8}. However, the encoder-decoder model can only generate definitions with the same complexity level, which is not enough to meet the needs of different scenarios.

